sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-41> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Enumerating simple axiom systems for a binary operator shows that the vast majority allow operators of many different forms (many models), so they are not about any one particular operator and are far from complete; only a few, such as those for logic, force essentially a single form.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Most simple axiom systems admit many different operator forms";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 12, “The Principle of Computational Equivalence”; section “Implications for Mathematics and Its Foundations” (from p. 772), p. 803. Scope: simple equational axiom systems for a single binary operator"
}
